Instead, let's try to consider the case when m=1. In this case, the only vertex cover is {u,v} where (u,v) is the edge. So A can be {u} and B can be {v}.

For the case when the graph is a star graph, with one central vertex and several leaves. For example, n=5, edges are (1,2), (1,3), (1,4), (1,5). A can be {1} and B can be {2,3,4,5}.

