    The problem requires us to check if repainting at most one cell can create a 2x2 square of the same color. We first check if a 2x2 square of the same color already exists. If it does, we output "YES". Otherwise, we iterate through each cell and repaint it, then check if a 2x2 square of the same color exists. If we find such a square after repainting any cell, we output "YES". If no such square exists after repainting any cell, we output "NO".

    The approach to check for a 2x2 square of the same color is to iterate through the 3x3 grid (because a 2x2 square can fit within a 4x4 grid in a 3x3 manner), and for each 2x2 square, check if all four cells have the same color.

